  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Cocycle Actions on Hidden Quantum Markov Models: Symmetry Protection and Topological Order — We develop a symmetry action framework for hidden quantum Markov models (HQMMs) tailored to\n\n**Cocycle Actions on Hidden Quantum Markov Models: Symmetry Protection and Topological Order**\n\n*Abdessatar Souissi*\n\n17 pp, 6 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We develop a symmetry action framework for hidden quantum Markov models (HQMMs) tailored to one-dimensional quantum spin systems and symmetry-protected topological (SPT) phases. In our setting, a symmetry group G acts projectively on the hidden (virtual) degrees of freedom and linearly on the physical observation space, yielding a global HQMM state that is invariant under the combined action of G for both conventional and causal (input– output) structures. We show that such symmetry actions are naturally classified by a group- cohomology 2-cocycle [ω] ∈H2(G, U(1)), in direct analogy with the standard cohomological classification of one-dimensional bosonic SPT phases via projective edge representations.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; Introduction; Cocycle Actions and Symmetry Protection in HQM; Application to AKLT's Symmetry-Protected Topol; Discussion and Outlook; Appedix: Hidden Quantum Markov Models",
      "lang": "en",
      "state": "draft",
